@startuml activity-async-text-input
'' PlantUML over Mermaid because this is a control flow with two INDEPENDENT lifetimes running against one
'' another — a keystroke's synchronous path and a sliced background job that outlives it — and PlantUML's
'' fork/partition plus per-step fills express that; Mermaid's flowchart cannot show the cancellation edge
'' without inventing a node for it. Literal palette hexes come from _vv-theme.iuml: teal #2D9574 renderer/
'' view, blue #4F97D7 re-frame, blue-violet #7590DB app-db, green #67B11D the DOM, red #E0211D the defect.
!include _vv-theme.iuml

title Asynchronous text input — one keystroke, two lifetimes (ADR-0033)

|#E3F2ED|the keystroke (synchronous, must finish in microseconds)|
start
:browser inserts the character
into the field's DOM value; <<#C7E8DE>>
:async-input **on-change**; <<#C7E8DE>>
note right
  The field's value is owned LOCALLY from
  here on. `draft` shadows the model, and the
  value is recorded in `pending` so the model
  echoing it back is recognised as ours and
  not mistaken for an external push.
end note
:dispatch a CHEAP event
(assoc-in and nothing else); <<#C4D9EB>>
:arm the shared debounce
**scheduler/debounce!**; <<#C4D9EB>>
stop

|#E8F0F8|the work (asynchronous, sliced, cancellable)|
start
:debounce lands
(one live timer per key —
re-arming REPLACES it); <<#C4D9EB>>

if (a valid flattened\nbuffer is cached?) then (yes — the common case)
  :reuse it; <<#D7EEC1>>
else (no)
  fork
    :**slice!** ::collect
    walk the DOM, feed the
    incremental buffer builder; <<#D7EEC1>>
    note right
      Keyed SEPARATELY from matching, and
      deliberately NOT cancelled when the query
      changes: the buffer depends only on the
      DOM. Cancelling it per keystroke meant a
      large document never finished flattening
      while the user typed.
    end note
    :store the buffer, stamped with
    the mutation counter it was built at; <<#D7EEC1>>
  end fork
endif

fork
  :**slice!** ::match
  scan (native indexOf), then
  build Ranges in batches; <<#D7EEC1>>
fork again
  -[#E0211D]-> next keystroke arrives;
  :**cancel!** ::match
  the superseded job stops
  between slices and reports nothing; <<#F0C0BF>>
  detach
end fork

:paint highlights, scroll to the first match; <<#D7EEC1>>
:publish the count into app-db; <<#C5CFEA>>
stop

legend right
  |= &#160;&#160;&#160; |= meaning |
  |<#C7E8DE>| renderer / view |
  |<#C4D9EB>| re-frame event, effect, scheduler |
  |<#C5CFEA>| app-db |
  |<#D7EEC1>| DOM work (walk, Ranges, highlights) |
  |<#F0C0BF>| cancellation — the superseded path |
  The invariant: **no step in the lower lane occupies the main thread for more**
  **than the frame budget without yielding**, and every one of them is abandoned
  the moment the next character arrives.
endlegend

@enduml
